1
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:08,055
Every week, a project manager spends hours collecting status from mail,

2
00:00:08,075 --> 00:00:12,593
meetings, chats and SharePoint, and still finds the risks too late.

3
00:00:12,893 --> 00:00:16,870
In the next few minutes, you will build a PM Agent in

4
00:00:16,890 --> 00:00:21,238
Microsoft 365 Copilot that does the collecting for you.

5
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:27,121
A weekly status draft, early warnings on risks, and every finding traced to its source.

6
00:00:28,021 --> 00:00:29,658
First, what is an agent?

7
00:00:29,678 --> 00:00:32,351
A normal prompt is a one-time question.

8
00:00:32,371 --> 00:00:37,198
You type, Copilot answers, and next time you start again from zero.

9
00:00:37,398 --> 00:00:40,748
An agent is Copilot set up once for a specific job.

10
00:00:40,768 --> 00:00:45,902
It has its own instructions, the knowledge it may use, and ready-made prompts.

11
00:00:45,922 --> 00:00:50,351
It keeps its role and follows your rules, every time you use it.

12
00:00:51,151 --> 00:00:52,460
So why is that better?

13
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:58,200
With a normal prompt, you re-type the context every week, the answer changes with your wording,

14
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:02,589
nothing is checked against your rules, and it stays in your own chat.

15
00:01:02,789 --> 00:01:07,909
With an agent, the context is built in, the output has the same structure every week,

16
00:01:07,929 --> 00:01:12,724
every finding comes with its source, and your whole project team can use it.

17
00:01:12,924 --> 00:01:15,800
Set it up once, and it pays you back every week.

18
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:18,924
Here is how your PM Agent works.

19
00:01:18,944 --> 00:01:23,881
It reads the places where your project actually lives: your Outlook email,

20
00:01:23,901 --> 00:01:30,465
your Teams meetings and their transcripts, your Teams chats, and the project’s SharePoint site.

21
00:01:30,565 --> 00:01:34,187
From them, it prepares three things: the weekly status draft,

22
00:01:34,207 --> 00:01:38,287
risk alerts, and the decisions and actions you might have missed.

23
00:01:38,387 --> 00:01:39,609
You stay in charge.

24
00:01:39,629 --> 00:01:43,229
The agent prepares, and the project manager decides.

25
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,433
Before you start, check four things.

26
00:01:46,483 --> 00:01:50,878
One: a Copilot Premium license with Agent Builder activated.

27
00:01:50,978 --> 00:01:55,052
Two: access to the project’s SharePoint site and Teams channels.

28
00:01:55,072 --> 00:01:57,830
The agent can only see what you can see.

29
00:01:57,930 --> 00:02:01,395
Three: transcription switched on for your project meetings,

30
00:02:01,415 --> 00:02:03,918
so the agent can read what was decided.

31
00:02:04,018 --> 00:02:06,514
And four: agreement on data rules.

32
00:02:06,534 --> 00:02:10,878
Project content only, and no personal or HR information.

33
00:02:11,878 --> 00:02:12,597
Step one.

34
00:02:12,617 --> 00:02:17,526
In Microsoft 365 Copilot, select New agent in the left pane.

35
00:02:17,546 --> 00:02:22,510
You can also open the Agent Store and select Create agent.

36
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:23,597
Step two.

37
00:02:23,617 --> 00:02:24,947
Agent Builder opens.

38
00:02:24,967 --> 00:02:29,132
You could start from a template, such as Project Delta Digest,

39
00:02:29,152 --> 00:02:31,495
or describe your agent in the chat.

40
00:02:31,515 --> 00:02:36,372
For full control, select Skip, and go straight to the Configure page.

41
00:02:36,472 --> 00:02:40,225
Select the pencil next to New Agent to give it a clear name,

42
00:02:40,245 --> 00:02:43,840
such as Project Pulse, and add a one-line description.

43
00:02:44,340 --> 00:02:46,105
Step three: the instructions.

44
00:02:46,125 --> 00:02:48,013
This is the heart of the agent.

45
00:02:48,033 --> 00:02:52,664
Tell it who it works for, what to produce, and the rules it must follow.

46
00:02:52,764 --> 00:02:56,033
Ask for a weekly status with a proposed rating,

47
00:02:56,053 --> 00:02:59,951
milestones, top risks, decisions, actions and open asks.

48
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:02,191
Require a source for every line.

49
00:03:02,211 --> 00:03:07,169
And make it flag conflicts and gaps, instead of smoothing them over.

50
00:03:07,269 --> 00:03:11,359
Finally, list the risk signals to watch for: a date that slips,

51
00:03:11,379 --> 00:03:17,319
a dependency that is overdue, or a reassuring “should be fine” about something critical.

52
00:03:17,419 --> 00:03:22,629
Suggest improvements can sharpen your wording, but read every change before you keep it.

53
00:03:23,129 --> 00:03:24,498
Step four: knowledge.

54
00:03:24,518 --> 00:03:28,333
By default, the agent can already search your cloud files,

55
00:03:28,353 --> 00:03:32,234
your Outlook mailbox, and your Teams meetings and messages.

56
00:03:32,254 --> 00:03:37,524
Select Add knowledge to focus it on the project’s SharePoint site and key files,

57
00:03:37,544 --> 00:03:39,794
like the plan and the risk log.

58
00:03:39,894 --> 00:03:43,602
Keep Outlook and Teams switched on, and switch web search off,

59
00:03:43,622 --> 00:03:46,468
so answers come only from your work content.

60
00:03:46,968 --> 00:03:47,590
Step five.

61
00:03:47,610 --> 00:03:55,297
Scroll down to Suggested prompts, and give each one a title and a message, so anyone can run the routine with one click:

62
00:03:55,317 --> 00:04:02,710
draft this week’s status, show new risks since Monday, and list decisions and actions from this week’s meetings.

63
00:04:03,210 --> 00:04:04,425
Step six: test it.

64
00:04:04,445 --> 00:04:08,475
Switch to the Preview tab and run the weekly status prompt.

65
00:04:08,495 --> 00:04:10,122
Then check three things.

66
00:04:10,142 --> 00:04:11,632
Is every line sourced?

67
00:04:11,652 --> 00:04:13,142
Are conflicts flagged?

68
00:04:13,162 --> 00:04:15,696
Is anything confidential left out?

69
00:04:15,796 --> 00:04:20,148
When a test fails, add one rule to the instructions and run it again.

70
00:04:20,648 --> 00:04:22,644
Step seven: make it a routine.

71
00:04:22,664 --> 00:04:28,827
Agent Builder agents run only when you ask, so book a short recurring slot in your calendar:

72
00:04:28,847 --> 00:04:34,002
the weekly status every Friday morning, and a quick risk check every morning.

73
00:04:34,022 --> 00:04:37,313
One click on a suggested prompt does the rest.

74
00:04:37,413 --> 00:04:40,509
For automatic alerts, without opening the agent,

75
00:04:40,529 --> 00:04:45,858
ask your Copilot Studio team to rebuild it with a schedule or an event trigger.

76
00:04:46,358 --> 00:04:47,050
Step eight.

77
00:04:47,070 --> 00:04:49,056
Select Create at the top right,

78
00:04:49,076 --> 00:04:53,521
then share the agent with your project team, or keep it for yourself.

79
00:04:53,541 --> 00:04:58,077
Each person only ever sees the content they already have access to.

80
00:04:59,077 --> 00:05:01,024
Here is what that looks like.

81
00:05:01,044 --> 00:05:04,416
On Tuesday morning, the daily risk check flags it:

82
00:05:04,436 --> 00:05:09,979
the load board has slipped from week 48 to week 50, according to a supplier email.

83
00:05:09,999 --> 00:05:12,234
It is not in the risk log yet.

84
00:05:12,334 --> 00:05:17,751
The alert names the source, suggests an owner, and proposes an update to the risk log.

85
00:05:17,771 --> 00:05:19,804
You decide what happens next.

86
00:05:20,304 --> 00:05:26,104
On Friday, one click gives you the status draft: sourced, structured, with conflicts flagged.

87
00:05:26,124 --> 00:05:29,420
You review it in fifteen minutes instead of compiling

88
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:32,456
it for three hours, set the rating, and send.

89
00:05:33,456 --> 00:05:34,879
Keep five guardrails.

90
00:05:34,899 --> 00:05:37,351
The agent respects your permissions.

91
00:05:37,371 --> 00:05:39,275
Every line names its source.

92
00:05:39,295 --> 00:05:42,778
The project manager owns every rating and decision.

93
00:05:42,798 --> 00:05:45,389
No personal data goes into the output.

94
00:05:45,409 --> 00:05:48,631
And a person checks before anything is sent.

95
00:05:49,431 --> 00:05:50,680
The agent gathers.

96
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:51,676
You decide.

97
00:05:52,476 --> 00:05:57,886
Build your PM Agent this week, and give your Fridays back to the work that matters.
